  "notes": "Piano solo on ONE grand staff (brace). A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" with 2 staves; it must NOT be split into right/left hand parts, and the second right-hand voice in bars 13-16 must stay inside the piano part (voice 2), not become a new part. DAMAGE (holes-staple): Filing damage: mild 2 ISO punch holes in the margin (show the white lid); scan 3 US holes (black, lid open) + a staple at the top-left; severe 4 holes centred 1 mm left of the staff start (they bite into braces/brackets, the system-start barline and possibly the left edge of a clef where they meet a staff) + staple + folded top-right corner. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Severe: where a hole meets a system its left end (brace/bracket/start barline, part of the clef) is physically missing; the folded corner can hide header text (composer/arranger). Music content is unchanged and the truth is complete."
 },
